      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tactical edge",
          "heading": "France beat Argentina 45-17 as Antoine Dupont's scrum move yields two tries",
          "body": "Antoine Dupont, not Matthieu Jalibert, ran the scrum launch that unlocked the Pumas in the 45-17 win at the Stade de France, Midi Olympique's breakdown shows. The same first-phase move put Mickaël Guillard over for the opening try and sent Émilien Gailleton in at the 64th minute for the bonus point that clinched a final against the Springboks. Kalvin Gourgues said Argentina's defence tended to narrow, especially near the line, which let France go wide by playing in behind."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland captain Dan Sheehan's yellow upgraded to red card",
          "body": "Wallabies beat Wales 29-26, ending losing run. South Africa make seven changes, starting Libbok and Reinach for final. All Blacks lose Luke Jacobson to Bayonne."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's hearing",
          "heading": "Captain Dan Sheehan's yellow upgraded to red after Ireland beat Springboks 20-17",
          "body": "Andy Farrell is sweating on his skipper before this week's Nations Championship finale against Australia at Twickenham. Sheehan was sin-binned for a croc-roll on Marco van Staden eight minutes from time on Saturday, before the foul play review officer made it a red, and the IRFU have yet to learn when his disciplinary hearing will be held. Otherwise there are no new injuries. \"We've got a full squad of fit bodies, which is great,\" said assistant coach Andrew Goodman, with Farrell naming his matchday squad on Wednesday afternoon."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wallabies beat Wales 29-26, ending losing run",
          "body": "South Africa make seven changes, starting Libbok and Reinach for final. All Blacks lose Luke Jacobson to Bayonne."
