    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Try record",
          "heading": "Darcy Graham reaches 41 Scotland tries in 67-5 win over Japan",
          "body": "Saturday's Nations Championship hat-trick at Murrayfield brought the wing's 39th, 40th and 41st international tries, extending his own Scotland record. He opened the scoring by hacking on after the visitors spilled Jamie Dobie's box-kick, and closed it in the 79th minute. Between those, he chased his own kick through and offloaded for Liam McConnell's second try, and Planet Rugby credited him with setting the tone in front of a 67,000 sell-out."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland captain Dan Sheehan's yellow upgraded to red card",
          "body": "Wallabies beat Wales 29-26, ending losing run. South Africa make seven changes, starting Libbok and Reinach for final. All Blacks lose Luke Jacobson to Bayonne."
