    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Midfield praise",
          "heading": "Tom Shanklin hails Eddie James a 'revelation' in Wales's emerging attack",
          "body": "Speaking on BBC Scrum V, the former Wales centre said James had \"been a revelation\" since being thrown in at Test level, and predicted he would be \"in that Welsh team for a long, long time as long as he's fit.\" James started all three November Tests, including Saturday's 26-29 defeat by Australia. Shanklin credited Matt Sherratt's attacking work and singled out Louis Rees-Zammit, who has scored in consecutive Tests after an eight-match drought."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland captain Dan Sheehan's yellow upgraded to red card",
