    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-24",
      "edition": "Tuesday 24 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "French verdict",
          "heading": "Rugbyrama calls Pumas brave but largely devoid of talent in 45-17 loss",
          "body": "France beat Argentina 45-17 at the Stade de France on Saturday, and Midi Olympique's Marc Duzan, writing for Rugbyrama, called the Pumas courageous but largely devoid of talent. His report conceded the visitors dominated the set scrum and answered Mickaël Guillard's opener through Justo Piccardo, Montpellier's hefty centre. France hooker Peato Mauvaka, interviewed by Rugbyrama, admitted frustration at the penalties his pack conceded at scrum time. Argentina's next assignment is Scotland at Twickenham, for seventh place."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland captain Dan Sheehan's yellow upgraded to red card",
